    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a senior localization quality reviewer. Evaluate ONE translated segment using MQM-style error annotation.\n\nSource (English): {{ $json.source }}\nTarget locale: {{ $json.locale }}\nTranslation: {{ $json.target }}\n\nError categories: Accuracy, Fluency, Terminology, Style, Locale convention, Other.\nSeverity levels:\n- Minor: noticeable but does not affect meaning or usability.\n- Major: changes or obscures meaning, or would make a reader stumble.\n- Critical: misleads the reader in a way that could cause harm, legal or safety exposure, or offense. Any translation that is incomplete (stops mid-sentence or drops a clause that changes the claim) is Critical, even if the remaining text is correct.\n\nRules:\n- Flag only errors a professional reviewer would flag. Preferential rewording is not an error.\n- Do not invent errors to look thorough. A clean segment gets error_count 0 and highest_severity \"None\".\n- For each error, quote the exact target span, then give the category, severity and a one-line reason.\n- Set judge_confidence to \"low\" if any call depends on context you don't have (ambiguous source, regional variant, missing glossary). Otherwise \"high\".\n\nReturn only the JSON object. issues_summary is a single string with one entry per error, formatted as:\n[Severity/Category] \"span\" - reason | [Severity/Category] \"span\" - reason",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
